<item><title>Gibba pledges religious salaries and Central River agriculture revival</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/gm/gibba-pledges-religious-salaries-and-central-river-8fb11a/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/gm/gibba-pledges-religious-salaries-and-central-river-8fb11a/</guid><category>Gambia</category><description>The independent candidate says he would pay imams and Christian leaders and restore farming in the Central River Region if elected on 5 December.</description><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 11:27:40 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/gm.jpg" length="31578" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/gm.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Diaspora members of Darboe&apos;s party return home to campaign before December 5 vote</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/gm/diaspora-members-of-darboe-s-party-return-home-to-campaign-4b8b9e/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/gm/diaspora-members-of-darboe-s-party-return-home-to-campaign-4b8b9e/</guid><category>Gambia</category><description>Dozens of diaspora members of the United Democratic Party (UDP) have come back to The Gambia to join the nationwide tour of opposition candidate Ousainou Darboe against President.</description><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 02:10:10 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/gm.jpg" length="31578" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/gm.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
